WEBVTT

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.780
All right! Let's start by playing catch, okay?

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.780
Okay!

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.280
Chiyo, will you come with me for pitching practice?
Izumi, let's go.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.320
Yeah.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:39.160
S-Sure.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:39.700
Let's start out lightly.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:40.410
It's been a while, so I wonder if it'll go well.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.030
Yeah.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.200
It's been a while, so I wonder if it'll go well.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.330
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Huh? Where did I leave my glove?

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.580
Mihashi!

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.750
Was there something you wanted to say before?

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:53.340
Be—

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.920
When Abe was talking, after the "I-I..." part.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:01.550
Abe said, "'I can still pitch,' right?"

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:02.760
What?

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.270
Oh, nothing.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:08.640
I just thought Mihashi looked like he wanted to say something, you know?

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:09.770
Like what?

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:13.480
It's probably nothing. In that case, you don't have to bother.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.150
What're you talking about?

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.650
It's nothing.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.900
I-I...

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.830
In the last game, Abe told me to ch-change.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.120
He did, didn't he?

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.170
But he only said that to shake you up.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.460
To put it simply, it was a lie, wasn't it?

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.130
I-I get it.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.590
Get what? Ah, that it was a lie?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.920
That's good.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.590
Because I didn't understand.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.010
Huh? Abe's sleeping...

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.520
Not doing things as he said... I regret it.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:50.020
He yelled pretty loudly, so it's no
surprise that you'd take it seriously.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.980
I wonder if I'll end up doing more things I'll regret?

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.860
Of course you will. Tons more.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:59.700
Like playing Power Pro for three
hours straight again or something.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.780
Are you saying you might not get off the mound even if you're told to?

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:11.460
If Abe says I'm no good, then that's when it's over for me.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.960
So... However... But...

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:21.800
If I don't listen to what you say,
I want you to stop catching my pitches.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.390
If you do that, I should come to my senses.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.680
Because there's no point in me pitching alone.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.980
Ehm...

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:32.900
Um...

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.310
Just in case you didn't know,

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:40.190
if you slip up and we lose, it won't be because you didn't sub out.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:45.990
Oki and Hanai aren't at a level where they can do anything in an official match yet, so...

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:52.330
if you can't pitch, then it's natural that
we'd lose... is what he meant to say, right?

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.580
Yeah, that's it.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:58.090
That's why we want to try to keep that from happening.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:58.840
Right, Abe?

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.340
Yeah!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.340
You three over there! Stop messing around!

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.220
Sorry!

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:07.970
I'll head over to Hanai.
We'll do it with three people.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.350
Okay.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.940
You think about a lot of things, don't you?

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:21.240
I... misunderstood... again... so...

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.070
I won't say any more.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:27.830
Wrong! You should say more!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.660
He's still doing it.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.950
Blockhead!

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.790
Geez, I can't believe you!

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.080
I'm sorry.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.330
The reason why Mihashi is so obsessive about the mound...

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:40.590
It's only a theory, but rather than being bullied,

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:46.300
I think Mihashi was completely ignored in middle school.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:52.310
Back then, he was treated as though he
didn't exist, and felt like an invisible man.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.560
But on the mound, you can't
start until the pitcher throws.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.940
While standing on the mound,
you know that you truly matter.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.320
If he gave up the mound, his essence would disappear.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.790
Despite being bound by various
contradictions and self-doubt,

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.080
and even while becoming a black sheep,

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.080
Mihashi never let go of the
mound during middle school.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.000
Coach, it curves! It curves!

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.290
But he just said he'd give it up!
To the outside now.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.250
Okay

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:24.920
If he still feels like he belongs here even if he gives up the mound, that's great.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.180
Here I go!

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:26.550
Okay!

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.550
Well, it's all just speculation, I guess.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.850
Rock! Paper! Scissors!

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:38.810
Crap!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.440
You better get the first defense!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.280
But it's not like I can do anything about Rock-Paper-Scissors, right!?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.400
Just as we said yesterday...

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.610
All right.
But it's not like I can do anything about Rock-Paper-Scissors, right!?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.070
We'll take the first offense.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.030
Let's have a good game.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:51.910
Thank you very much!

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.160
Thank goodness!

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.090
They're taking the first offense after playing through extra innings in two games?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.340
Maybe they have some sort of philosophy, but...

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.930
most likely, they haven't really thought it out.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:14.140
The coach is new to baseball, and their
gameplay seems completely unplanned.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.390
Hanai!

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.100
Yes!

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.850
We'll be going ahead.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:19.520
Okay!

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.060
Do you really think we can pull off a shut-out today?

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.280
Well...

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.070
W-Whether we can do it or not, either way... we'll go for it.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:31.740
Just now, looking at Sakitama's coach and captain...

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.780
I thought, "We can do it!"

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.870
Hanai, you'll become a hero today!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.300
Top of the first inning.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:48.760
Sakitama's first batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Tanaka.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.260
First inning! Let's shut them down!

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.220
Yeah!

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.680
Let them hit it, Pitcher!
Sakitama's first batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Tanaka.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.680
A hero.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:04.110
Shortstop!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.190
Out!

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.990
Nice catch!

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.150
A hero...

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.240
Nice catch!

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:14.740
Nice, second!

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:16.620
First!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.160
I got it! I got it!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:18.750
Out!

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.330
She's telling me to hit, right?

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.040
Nice, first! Nice pitching!

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:25.920
Gotcha.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:32.630
All right, let's go! For the first inning, two or more runs!

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:33.390
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.600
Listen up! In order to gain momentum,
this inning is important.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.350
Two or more runs?

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.890
The team that beat Tousei, huh?

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.060
Bottom of the first inning for Nishiura's offense.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.190
Ready!

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.730
Bottom of the first inning for Nishiura's offense.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:43.980
Bring it on!

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.150
First batter. First baseman: Number 5, Tajima.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.940
First and third are in fixed positions.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:53.990
First!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:55.950
Safe!

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.660
Tajima, that rascal! His bunt is good too.
Looking good!

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.250
With him, there won't be a double play.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:01.960
They'll get around to me.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.500
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.420
Ready!

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.290
Second batter. Second baseman: Number 4, Sakaeguchi.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.550
They got someone on base so easily.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.630
The second batter will probably bunt it too.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.590
I guess it'll be a showdown with the third batter?

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:16.050
Ball!

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.140
As I thought, this person's form isn't solid.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:24.600
It's not persistent, but it feels like he hasn't been pitching for very long.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.020
Safe!

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.860
He'll even throw with that much lead-off?

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.990
There's no way you could nail him with such a small gap!

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.240
Pitcher, pitcher!

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.240
Wasn't that a risky throw?
Play!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:37.320
Wasn't that a risky throw?

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:37.830
Regardless of the fact that there've been no bad throws,

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.370
Nice run-back!

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.790
Good job getting back!
Regardless of the fact that there've been no bad throws,

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:41.620
I don't get the point of a pickoff that can't throw out the runner.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:42.700
That was a fast throw.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:43.910
Yeah.
I don't get the point of a pickoff that can't throw out the runner.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.960
Batter's on base.
On top of being annoying, it draws out the game and irritates people.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.210
Be careful!

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:47.250
Don't tell me that's what they're aiming for.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.460
Let's take it easy!

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.840
You can do it!
Don't tell me that's what they're aiming for.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:54.300
We're lucky to discern the catcher's
rhythm before going to second base.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.510
Until we get one strike, it's Tajima's time.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.510
We're going for a shut-out today after all, huh?

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.850
I have to use my legs to stir things up!

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.900
That's a huge lead-off. Should I throw it?

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.860
It's all right, Senpai! Let's retire this batter!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:12.190
You'll throw it for me, won't you?

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.070
You love pickoffs.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:17.450
Then let's go; I'm tired anyway. I'll leave it to the...

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:18.410
Go!

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.660
...young guys!

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:21.660
All right!

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.210
He went back?

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:26.830
That was close.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.830
With this timing, it'd be an out.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.040
Makes your heart race!

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.510
From here on, let's go by orthodox methods.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.670
We'll take the first point carefully.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.340
First!

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:39.550
Out!

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:40.470
He's safe. What a lifesaver.
Nice batting!

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:41.430
Yeah.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.020
He's safe. What a lifesaver.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:46.810
Third batter. Third baseman: Number 8, Izumi.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:47.730
All right!

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.020
Now then, Izumi, huh?

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.480
Only right-handed batters have swung here.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:53.360
He wants to hit it.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:54.190
One out!

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:57.860
I'd go with a bunt if we were playing it safe, but let's see if he can do it.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.530
First pitch will be a strike.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.410
She left it up to me! It really feels like I'm third batter.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.580
Izumi's going to hit?

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:07.870
Whether Izumi makes it or goes out, I'll definitely score some runs!

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:10.130
I'm lucky to be third batter here.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:12.840
With Tajima running and Hanai batting after me, I can relax.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.210
Or at least I can be more positive.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.800
Fastball to the inside? That's a no-go.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.890
This guy was moved from first batter to third batter.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.680
The outside is fine, but a strike is no good!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:32.650
That's right. I want to put one ball outside and avert their attention.

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:39.570
It's fine since I set up the pitch order, but you never remember any of my preferences at all.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.530
And I'm tired of shaking my head!

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.080
Outside? Is it far? It's good! Swing!

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:44.830
It'll go out!

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:46.790
No...

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:48.410
Fair!

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:49.160
It's a long hit!

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:50.870
Tajima, run!

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.090
Gotta go pick up the bat and direct the runner!

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.550
First point!

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.010
Izumi, go, go! You can make third base!

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.300
Right! To third!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.390
Shit, I was slow!

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:02.720
Hurry it up!

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.720
Izumi, slide! Left! Left!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.270
Safe! Safe!

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:09.520
Third base!

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.270
One, two. Nice batting!

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:16.270
Hey, hey! Let's try saying "Nice batting!"

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:16.730
What?

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.440
We'll say it on two, okay?

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:19.400
One, two...

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.200
What?
One, two...

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.320
Nice batting!

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:25.990
Oh goodness, we're all over the place!

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.790
What are they laughing about?

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:30.660
Fourth batter. Center fielder: Number 9, Hanai.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:32.000
One out!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.920
Um...

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:39.340
My target hasn't changed. I'm going to score points!

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.800
The game is moving!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.930
We've hit the ball and scored a point. The flow of the game is in our favor.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.220
On top of that, we have a runner on third and our fourth batter is up.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.310
The opposing side's defense should be on guard.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.270
S-Squeeze?

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.730
I let myself relax!

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:55.440
Ready!

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.690
I need to stop getting so worked up; it's way too uncool.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.190
Focus, focus.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:04.360
We need at least two points. I can't ruin this chance.

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:04.990
All right, I've gotta give the
impression that I'm going for a hit.

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:06.240
Play!

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.370
Bring it!

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:08.080
All right, I've gotta give the
impression that I'm going for a hit.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:12.540
Daichi's just like this guy. They're only first years, but they're really big.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.040
Always so inconvenient.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:16.130
Squeeze?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.040
Nice, Hanai!

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.040
They got us!

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:18.670
First!

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:19.800
Second point!

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:20.630
All right!
Out!

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:21.260
All right!

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:23.220
Fifth batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Suyama.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.380
Nice bunt.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:27.100
Yeah, I'm glad it didn't get away from me.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.770
They really weren't prepared for a squeeze at all.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:34.850
Is it because I'm the fourth batter? In any case, we scored a point.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.690
For the next at-bat too...

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.190
Don't be satisfied.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.030
About what?

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:43.700
You are?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:44.240
Good luck!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.780
What? Satisfied?

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.950
Why not? I got us one point, didn't I?

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:52.330
Of course, I could aim for higher. I mean, I got out and all.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.920
And if I'd gotten a home run,
we would've scored two points.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.670
But the coach's directions were to go for a squeeze.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.880
Am I no good because I was told to squeeze?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.420
But in that situation,

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:06.840
no matter who the batter was, wouldn't Coach Momo tell them to do a squeeze?

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:07.890
Strike!

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.850
Here!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.270
Anyone except you.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:13.770
Nice pitch!

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:14.730
Strike!

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.480
They're leading by two points?

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:20.690
But next is Daichi.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.730
Sakura! Hit that ball!

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:24.400
Good luck, Daichi!

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.450
Yes!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.610
Daichi sure is popular.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:30.200
I'm batting before him, you know.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.160
It's number 5.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:37.120
I'll set up inside the box, so throw it farther out than my mitt.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:40.790
I don't think it'll happen, but just in case, throw it where he can't reach it, okay?

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:42.300
O-Okay.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:46.130
Also, even if the old men up in the stands heckle you, don't pay them any attention, okay?

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:51.260
The jeering for a walk is directed at me,
since you're only pitching as I tell you to.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.100
I-I...

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:54.970
Mihashi, I'll take your gear.

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:56.390
Thank you.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:57.600
What?

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:02.020
It's jeering for me! I'm fine.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.610
That so?

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.360
Well, if you're fine, then that's good.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:09.200
We'll make up for the amount we slack on number 5 with the others.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.030
I'm counting on you!

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:11.780
Y-Yeah!

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:14.700
Being counted on makes me happy.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.790
When I'm happy, I get filled with strength.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:19.920
I have to walk him because I'm powerless.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.250
If I had the power to fight head-on,

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.420
I wouldn't have to do something as dangerous as a walk.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:30.180
Since I can't fight, I run. If I run, the people watching will get angry.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:33.430
But if I have to run, then I'll run.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.890
I can take heckling.

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.100
Nice pitch!

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:39.560
The team's ace can't give away hits!

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:44.860
Top of the second inning for Sakitama's offense.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.400
Fourth batter. Shortstop: Number 9, Oyama.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:51.110
There's no speed at all. All three people before me said it was easy to hit.

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:54.740
Most likely, the pitch was too slow and they couldn't get enough power on the hit,

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.200
so it went out.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.410
If I swing right, it should pass the infield.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:02.540
Fastball!

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:06.050
Out!

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:08.050
Nice pitch!
It popped up!

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.260
I really wanted to get on base before Daichi.

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:12.800
The fences are low in this stadium,
so maybe suddenly hitting past the fence...
Fifth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Sakura.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:13.640
Ready!

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.640
The fences are low in this stadium,
so maybe suddenly hitting past the fence...

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:16.600
Fifth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Sakura.

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:21.270
Hey, hey, hey!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:24.810
A walk?

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:26.320
Come on!

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:30.740
Pitcher, face the batter! Don't run away!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.360
That's cheating!

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:34.410
That's dirty!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.490
Is he doing that on purpose?

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:37.740
Probably.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.460
With the catcher standing up like that, isn't his turn at bat already over?

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:44.800
They're walking him off as a counter-measure.

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:46.790
Isn't Daichi awesome?

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:49.630
But will they do that for all of his at-bats?

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:51.720
It's possible.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.300
Isn't that really bad?

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:56.800
Ball four!

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.970
I couldn't hit it.

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:02.690
And I was so looking forward to it.
Seemed like such an easy ball to hit.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:04.150
Hi.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.810
H-Hi.

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.610
Where did you play in middle school?

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.320
Um, I played soccer in middle school.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.400
Really? Did you quit soccer?

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:17.120
No, Sakitama just doesn't have a soccer team.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.330
Then you didn't have a baseball team in middle school?

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:21.790
That's right!

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.870
Then you've only just started playing baseball!?

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:28.590
In elementary school, I played youth baseball!

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.960
Hey, casual speech is fine, you know.
I'm also a first year.

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:34.720
What? You should have told me earlier!

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.180
No whispering!

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:37.760
Yes! Sorry!

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.760
Kamimura, hit it!

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:40.430
Right!

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:42.770
What should I do? Should I bunt it?

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.230
Go ahead and hit it; it's an easy pitch to hit.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.070
All right. Down the middle!

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:52.860
Got it.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:53.570
Second!

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:54.240
Here!

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:55.200
Okay. First!

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:56.990
Out!

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.450
Double play!

00:16:58.450 --> 00:16:59.490
Nice pitching!

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:03.330
Geez, we finally had a chance.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.960
How pathetic.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.670
Sorry.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:08.840
Ryou, you got hooked by the inside corner?

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:11.250
It came down the middle, but it was a shootball.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.170
How about you, Tai?

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.050
It was down the middle for me too.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.760
Maybe it curved a little after all.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:19.930
Well, no one's been struck out yet. We're just getting started!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:20.760
Yeah.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:25.890
But if Daichi can't hit, our scoring power will be cut in half.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:29.400
In any case, we've got to focus on filling the bases before Daichi's turn at bat.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:31.690
We were heckled pretty badly.

00:17:31.690 --> 00:17:33.570
Y-Yeah. I'm fine.

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:37.360
It's all going according to plan over here.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.570
Y-Yes.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:42.330
Your grinning face worked to irritate them pretty well, too.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.040
Yes.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:46.410
We'll score some points and chase them into a corner once again.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.000
The heckling will continue to get worse, but that just means we're succeeding.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:54.260
No matter what they say, keep grinning, okay?

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:55.760
Y-Yeah.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:59.800
Sorry I'm late.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:00.640
Mrs. Abe.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:02.640
You're just in time to watch your son.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:04.810
That Taka!

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.310
What's wrong?

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:10.060
This morning during breakfast, he ate Shun's portion of eggs.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.780
More importantly, yesterday,
Taka was talking with his dad.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:19.700
When he asked, "Do you have a counter-measure for Sakitama's number 5?"

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.870
Taka replied, "We're walking him."

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.290
Then the two of them smirked.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:29.620
Does that mean it was something that Abe decided on?

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:32.500
Um, they did it.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.960
They really did it?

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.760
Wasn't the heckling terrible?

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:37.260
Uh, Mrs. Mihashi?

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.380
Y-Yes!

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:43.760
I'm sorry! Our son is always doing as he pleases.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.060
Mrs. Abe?
Not at all! Our son as well...

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:45.890
That's right.
Not at all! Our son as well...

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:50.600
No. No!

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:54.480
I'm guessing the pitcher is deciding the pitch order,

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:58.240
but the catcher's really making him shake his head too much.

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.110
You should make it easier on him.

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.620
After coming to the outside and inside, in order to let the last screw go...

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.120
One more ball to the inside!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:08.830
One of the things we wanted to check for stealing bases was left-handed batters.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:12.630
One, two. Nice batting!

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:17.550
During a previous game, they allowed a stolen base when a left-handed batter was at the plate.
Seventh batter. Right fielder: Number 3, Oki.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:18.510
Bunt.

00:19:18.510 --> 00:19:19.970
Sacrifice bunt.

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:21.340
Now!

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.800
He's running!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:23.430
Crap!

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.470
The runner came out from behind the batter.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.470
I'm not in a proper throwing stance!

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:28.640
Safe!

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.600
Just barely made it! With this,
we're on second base with no outs.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.230
Not bad, Abe. Awesome!

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:36.070
I thought he wouldn't be able to run.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.860
That Daichi...

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:41.820
I tell him every game that they might steal bases even if they set up for a bunt.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.830
He only remembers what he's been told during the current match.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:49.160
If he hadn't relaxed, we could've kept the number of stolen bases at zero.

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:52.870
All right.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.170
Out!

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:55.790
Eighth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:56.670
Ready!

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.130
Eighth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.420
Reiichi.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:00.130
Yes?

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.260
It's gonna be a squeeze. Move forward to field it.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.010
Okay.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:05.930
Here goes the first ball!

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:07.390
Ball.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.850
He wasn't waiting for the first pitch?

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.810
They were kind enough to give us a ball.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.310
The second ball—I'll just hold my stance.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.270
I'll try putting in the second ball.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:18.190
Ball.

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:21.780
Shit, I was thrown off by his stance!

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:25.570
No strikes, two balls. If I don't get one in, it'll be really tough later.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:31.410
But doesn't it seem like a count where they'd pull out a bunt?

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:32.830
Ball.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:36.540
Shit! He didn't do it!

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:45.890
I can't help thinking, "If only Daichi was
more reliable as catcher," in times like this.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.350
Whatever. Let's just let him walk.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.730
Ball four.

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:55.560
Now then, what should I do about Mihashi?

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.440
With a runner on first base, there's the
danger of a double play even if we bunt.

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:59.110
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.940
Since it's probably impossible for Mizutani to steal two bases,

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:05.400
should I have Mihashi strike out and bet on Tajima, who still can't swing?

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:09.120
Or should I ignore the danger of a
double play and let Mihashi swing?

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:15.040
My role is to bring Abe home.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:20.000
Instead of letting him strike out and
giving them an out, we'll let him hit it.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:23.090
Hitting?

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:26.050
Mizutani, it'll be a grounder. Run back.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:26.680
Got it.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:31.060
I'll let him hit a grounder and get first and second base out. Let's retire him.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.140
This batter's a lefty. Number nine!

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:37.270
Strike!

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.770
I swung too hard.

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:44.780
Is this all right?

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.450
If it's an infield grounder, they'll get a double play.

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:47.570
Does he understand that?

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.030
Third runner.

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:53.580
No, he's just looking at the third runner.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:57.500
He glared at me with such good timing;
it's as though he could read my thoughts.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:00.750
I want to hit too.

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:03.500
I want us to aim for a shut-out.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.920
I want to hit too.

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.630
I want to be a part of the shut-out too!

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:10.800
I want to score points!

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:46.570
Without losing confidence from the other team's heckling, they walk Sakura according to plan...

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:49.780
and hold down Sakitama at zero points in the bottom of the second inning.

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:54.620
The other team's pitcher, Ichihara, seems irritated somehow.

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:59.750
Also, there seems to be an air of unease over on Sakitama's side.

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:05.080
Will the captain, Oyama, be able to pull everything together properly?

00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:05.960
Next time:

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:06.880
Baseball is Tiring.

00:24:07.630 --> 00:24:09.380
Baseball is fun.
